  "identity": "GW keyword-Voltron tempo. The deck concentrates permanent size on one or two bodies - Travel Preparations gives four castings of two +1/+1 counters, Lunarch Mantle is a permanent +2/+2 with a repeatable evasion outlet, Gryff's Boon adds flying and buys itself back out of the graveyard - and then Odric, Lunarch Marshal converts that single enhanced creature into a whole-team effect: 'creatures you control gain first strike until end of turn if a creature you control has first strike. The same is true for flying, deathtouch, double strike, haste, hexproof, indestructible, lifelink, menace, reach, skulk, trample, and vigilance.' One Twinblade Geist makes the team double strike; a Gryff's Boon, Niblis of the Urn or Restoration Angel makes it fly; Thalia makes it first-strike. Underneath that it is a genuine tempo deck: four one-drops, fourteen two-drops, nine interaction spells, and Cathar Commando and Restoration Angel both have flash, so the turn it taps out is a turn it chose.",
